WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.000
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:00.020 --> 00:01.680
[Disclaimer: This series is created solely for entertainment purposes.

3
00:01.700 --> 00:03.350
All individuals, behaviors, places, and events depicted are entirely fictional,

4
00:03.370 --> 00:05.000
with no intention to represent or reference any organizations, departments, occupations, or individuals]

5
00:05.110 --> 00:06.960
But every time I dream,

6
00:07.310 --> 00:08.640
it's always about her.

7
00:11.330 --> 00:13.400
I used to be in here, didn't I?

8
00:13.860 --> 00:15.920
But my feelings say otherwise.

9
00:16.510 --> 00:17.990
I kissed you,

10
00:18.350 --> 00:20.400
because I don't want to be just friends.

11
00:21.130 --> 00:22.690
We still have hope.

12
00:23.220 --> 00:24.220
What hope?

13
00:24.240 --> 00:25.090
Chris...

14
00:25.450 --> 00:26.980
will never love Nadear.

15
00:27.610 --> 00:30.220
I'll help you out.

16
00:31.340 --> 00:33.690
I want you to remember.

17
00:33.910 --> 00:35.550
I'll make Chris

18
00:35.710 --> 00:36.970
mine...

19
00:37.490 --> 00:39.320
by any means necessary.

20
00:44.200 --> 00:45.120
[Several days ago]

21
00:45.140 --> 00:46.460
She's there.

22
00:47.340 --> 00:49.110
I can't believe

23
00:50.120 --> 00:52.300
that I'll get to see her again.

24
00:53.100 --> 00:54.760
She seems to enjoy working out, huh?

25
00:55.020 --> 00:56.600
If she isn't swimming,

26
00:56.620 --> 00:58.300
she'll usually come to this park to run.

27
01:00.110 --> 01:02.120
She really hasn't changed at all.

28
01:03.610 --> 01:04.610
It's different, though.

29
01:05.310 --> 01:06.720
She lost her memories.

30
01:08.710 --> 01:09.800
What do you think?

31
01:19.010 --> 01:20.900
Did she really forget about me?

32
01:24.000 --> 01:26.060
She didn't keep her promise.

33
01:30.000 --> 01:31.910
If she really has forgotten about me,

34
01:32.690 --> 01:34.410
maybe I can finally let this go.

35
01:37.780 --> 01:39.640
But I still want to make sure.

36
01:58.980 --> 02:00.040
Carissa...

37
02:00.400 --> 02:02.650
You really don't remember me?

38
02:41.540 --> 02:51.460
♫The rain keeps splashing beneath our cover,♫

39
02:51.480 --> 02:56.580
♫Once it was a special place for two lovers♫

40
02:56.600 --> 03:00.480
♫There was never enough room for the third♫

41
03:00.690 --> 03:06.690
♫Now, the rain soaks our hearts together♫

42
03:06.720 --> 03:16.440
♫The question that's trapped in my heart♫

43
03:16.460 --> 03:21.500
♫Maybe it's time for you to do your part♫

44
03:21.520 --> 03:25.800
♫Choose the one your heart truly desires♫

45
03:25.820 --> 03:34.460
♫Before the last raindrop falls, don't make me shed another tear♫

46
03:35.200 --> 03:43.280
♫Before the last raindrop falls, don't make me shed another tear♫

47
04:01.760 --> 04:03.160
I knew what love was

48
04:05.280 --> 04:06.920
when I first met you.

49
04:29.600 --> 04:31.050
Her touch...

50
04:32.340 --> 04:33.840
Her smell...

51
05:06.120 --> 05:06.770
Chris.

52
05:09.750 --> 05:10.990
I'll make things right

53
05:12.050 --> 05:13.290
in three months.

54
05:24.070 --> 05:24.850
Mm.

55
05:35.230 --> 05:36.850
I'll wait for you no matter how long it takes.

56
05:52.680 --> 05:53.260
Here.

57
05:59.690 --> 06:00.770
Thanks.

58
06:01.130 --> 06:01.790
Mm.

59
06:04.870 --> 06:06.160
What will you do next?

60
06:08.910 --> 06:10.430
It's just three months.

61
06:11.420 --> 06:13.410
It's nothing compared to the four years I've waited.

62
06:15.240 --> 06:17.580
You finally got her back, huh?

63
06:19.670 --> 06:21.380
I already did it once.

64
06:22.060 --> 06:23.560
Why can't I do it again?

65
06:25.640 --> 06:27.570
If everything ends well, that's good.

66
06:28.090 --> 06:29.260
But keep in mind

67
06:29.570 --> 06:31.290
if Nadear asked her this,

68
06:32.000 --> 06:33.170
it means

69
06:33.480 --> 06:35.090
she's already planned what she will do next.

70
06:35.870 --> 06:37.260
It's been four years,

71
06:37.700 --> 06:39.490
and Chris still came back to me.

72
06:40.210 --> 06:41.730
What can Nadear do?

73
06:42.980 --> 06:43.910
Hold Chris back.

74
06:44.570 --> 06:46.450
She managed to ask for three months.

75
06:46.610 --> 06:47.850
Don't you think

76
06:48.360 --> 06:50.280
that maybe she can keep asking for more time?

77
06:58.290 --> 06:59.750
Actually...

78
07:00.990 --> 07:02.490
Those three months

79
07:03.490 --> 07:05.270
aren't just important to Nadear.

80
07:07.870 --> 07:09.970
They're important to me too.

81
07:13.970 --> 07:15.440
I don't know

82
07:17.750 --> 07:19.260
if what we have between Chris and me

83
07:21.360 --> 07:22.680
is really "love,"

84
07:24.200 --> 07:25.990
or just an instinct.

85
07:27.160 --> 07:28.670
A feeling of nostalgia.

86
07:30.690 --> 07:31.790
So...

87
07:32.640 --> 07:33.860
How are they different?

88
07:35.380 --> 07:37.060
Because Chris lost her memories.

89
07:40.560 --> 07:42.990
If our love

90
07:43.250 --> 07:46.000
came from familiarity,

91
07:49.350 --> 07:51.480
Chris might not choose me.

92
07:58.980 --> 08:00.660
If over these three months,

93
08:03.210 --> 08:05.450
our love blooms once more...

94
08:07.090 --> 08:09.280
If it really is love,

95
08:12.970 --> 08:14.980
I won't care about her past again.

96
08:29.690 --> 08:31.360
Are you having a sleepover with your friends?

97
08:31.730 --> 08:32.360
Mm.

98
08:32.380 --> 08:33.720
That way, I'll get to leave my room.

99
08:34.370 --> 08:37.010
Tell your friends that you want to spend some time with your girlfriend.

100
08:38.780 --> 08:41.010
They'll think I'm avoiding them.

101
08:45.390 --> 08:46.930
You worry about what your friends think,

102
08:47.910 --> 08:49.780
but you don't worry if your girlfriend misses you?

103
08:51.340 --> 08:53.920
Her hair smells faintly of shampoo.

104
08:54.280 --> 08:55.330
Her hair is fine

105
08:55.770 --> 08:57.130
and smooth.

106
08:59.880 --> 09:02.760
She likes to tuck it behind her ears to keep it out of her face

107
09:03.660 --> 09:05.570
when she bends down to kiss me on the bed.

108
09:15.870 --> 09:16.570
Sun...

109
09:19.380 --> 09:20.190
Sun.

110
09:25.810 --> 09:26.770
Who is that?

111
09:32.860 --> 09:34.260
How did you get in here?

112
09:36.480 --> 09:38.770
I was worried you might have a nightmare,

113
09:39.150 --> 09:41.610
so I came in to check on you as usual.

114
09:43.500 --> 09:45.250
But what's happening between us isn't usual.

115
09:45.950 --> 09:48.480
But we still have three months to get back to how it used to be.

116
09:54.400 --> 09:55.810
And who is Sun?

117
10:00.920 --> 10:01.860
A friend.

118
10:06.160 --> 10:08.760
A friend who helped me come up with the flower dishes.

119
10:09.400 --> 10:12.840
I think you're so stressed about the flower dishes

120
10:16.300 --> 10:18.750
that you even dreamed about your friend.

121
10:23.050 --> 10:24.510
I think you should rest.

122
10:28.460 --> 10:29.760
Rest?

123
10:30.460 --> 10:31.240
Your work.

124
10:33.860 --> 10:34.860
Stop doing your work.

125
10:50.010 --> 10:51.880
You've treated me like a sick person

126
10:52.960 --> 10:54.440
for four whole years.

127
10:54.700 --> 10:56.760
Hasn't that been more than enough?

128
10:57.970 --> 10:59.640
- I'm just... - "Worried."

129
11:00.460 --> 11:01.460
"Want what's best for me."

130
11:02.570 --> 11:04.800
I've heard you say this hundreds of times now.

131
11:06.130 --> 11:08.020
You want me to act normal,

132
11:08.960 --> 11:11.760
but don't you realize our relationship was never normal to begin with?

133
11:29.930 --> 11:31.160
I'm going to see my friend.

134
11:40.770 --> 11:41.360
Here.

135
11:41.560 --> 11:42.470
Thanks.

136
11:44.930 --> 11:46.400
Everything is going smoothly.

137
11:46.420 --> 11:47.790
It should open on schedule.

138
11:49.090 --> 11:50.260
Well done.

139
11:54.430 --> 11:55.920
So when are you opening?

140
11:56.620 --> 11:58.140
Well, you said three more months.

141
12:03.190 --> 12:04.520
I know.

142
12:05.670 --> 12:07.780
I see you barely smiled today.

143
12:09.160 --> 12:10.670
You seem stressed.

144
12:11.500 --> 12:13.270
Is something bothering you?

145
12:15.800 --> 12:17.360
It's about my dream.

146
12:19.450 --> 12:20.960
Would you like to talk about it?

147
12:23.130 --> 12:23.960
Not yet.

148
12:25.630 --> 12:26.460
Alright,

149
12:27.570 --> 12:29.060
as long as you're happy.

150
12:31.260 --> 12:32.200
Okay.

151
12:34.440 --> 12:35.760
[Verity Skin Clinic]

152
12:36.800 --> 12:38.240
If I want to talk, I'll tell you.

153
12:38.770 --> 12:39.380
Mm.

154
12:47.560 --> 12:49.260
So it's really you, Sun.

155
12:52.570 --> 12:55.410
[Third Person]

156
12:56.614 --> 13:00.464
[Third Person]

157
13:02.894 --> 13:04.664
Sun, your junior.

158
13:05.264 --> 13:07.134
How was she doing

159
13:09.164 --> 13:10.524
after that accident four years ago?

160
13:11.364 --> 13:12.844
Her brain injury

161
13:13.454 --> 13:16.334
caused her to lose her memory temporarily.

162
13:16.804 --> 13:17.454
Does this mean

163
13:18.324 --> 13:19.254
she'll get better

164
13:19.454 --> 13:21.224
soon, right?

165
13:21.454 --> 13:22.164
Yes.

166
13:23.704 --> 13:24.984
But...

167
13:26.464 --> 13:27.674
We found that

168
13:28.344 --> 13:30.374
Sun has a tumor near her brainstem.

169
13:42.714 --> 13:44.294
When I first told you this,

170
13:45.184 --> 13:47.484
you said you were Sun's friend, didn't you?

171
13:47.754 --> 13:48.544
Yes,

172
13:50.204 --> 13:52.464
we went to the same high school.

173
13:54.184 --> 13:55.254
It's been four years.

174
13:56.454 --> 13:57.764
Why did you come back

175
13:57.784 --> 13:58.784
to ask me about this again?

176
13:59.194 --> 14:01.064
Back then, you said Sun's father

177
14:01.084 --> 14:03.054
took her overseas.

178
14:03.794 --> 14:04.564
Yes,

179
14:06.174 --> 14:07.854
she lost her memories,

180
14:09.794 --> 14:11.144
so her father took the opportunity

181
14:11.564 --> 14:13.264
to start her life anew over there.

182
14:15.114 --> 14:16.644
I think Sun got her memories back.

183
14:17.454 --> 14:18.974
If she's back...

184
14:21.874 --> 14:23.474
If she got her memories back and came back,

185
14:24.114 --> 14:26.214
why did no one know this?

186
14:35.874 --> 14:37.264
You feel like...

187
14:37.284 --> 14:39.024
you've known someone before?

188
14:41.754 --> 14:43.154
If you like someone,

189
14:43.554 --> 14:45.354
you can feel that way too.

190
14:46.214 --> 14:47.144
It's like...

191
14:50.354 --> 14:51.944
you've known each other for a long time.

192
14:52.964 --> 14:53.964
You've heard of it before, yeah?

193
14:56.744 --> 14:58.154
I think so too.

194
15:01.414 --> 15:02.444
That means you like her.

195
15:09.914 --> 15:10.954
I told you,

196
15:11.754 --> 15:13.134
I'm trying to uphold

197
15:13.574 --> 15:14.884
both my medical ethics

198
15:15.464 --> 15:16.464
and my code as a friend.

199
15:21.964 --> 15:23.634
I've felt that way ever since I first met her.

200
15:26.204 --> 15:27.894
What made you curious about this?

201
15:28.614 --> 15:29.844
I had a dream.

202
15:30.974 --> 15:33.414
And I started dreaming more as we had more physical contact.

203
15:33.984 --> 15:35.054
What are you curious about?

204
15:36.224 --> 15:38.054
Well, if I used to know her...

205
15:38.914 --> 15:40.464
What was our relationship like?

206
15:43.894 --> 15:44.944
Would you like me to help?

207
15:49.314 --> 15:50.354
I don't know...

208
15:51.274 --> 15:52.774
It feels so familiar.

209
15:53.954 --> 15:56.744
Familiar enough that I want to find the answer myself.

210
16:22.474 --> 16:23.474
Why...

211
16:24.654 --> 16:26.544
Why can't I find anything...?

212
16:33.624 --> 16:34.884
What are you looking for?

213
16:38.074 --> 16:39.694
Are you looking for someone named Sun?

214
16:44.704 --> 16:46.054
Did you know

215
16:47.374 --> 16:49.564
why I'm suspicious of you?

216
16:55.884 --> 16:57.364
Because you dreamed,

217
17:01.314 --> 17:02.944
but it wasn't the same.

218
17:31.434 --> 17:32.264
Nadear...

219
17:40.074 --> 17:41.074
Are you tired?

220
17:42.144 --> 17:43.654
Not that much.

221
17:44.444 --> 17:45.834
Thank you.

222
17:45.854 --> 17:46.674
Let me massage you.

223
17:47.274 --> 17:48.154
Yes,

224
17:48.844 --> 17:51.864
back then, when I dreamed about our past,

225
17:52.294 --> 17:54.754
I'd love Nadear even more.

226
17:58.774 --> 18:00.054
I dreamed...

227
18:05.194 --> 18:06.444
but it wasn't the same?

228
18:07.954 --> 18:10.254
Can you make an effort

229
18:11.654 --> 18:14.464
for these three months we still have?

230
18:44.434 --> 18:45.864
My clinic is ready.

231
18:45.884 --> 18:47.554
Would you like to come see it?

232
19:01.554 --> 19:04.044
Why do you want to open a beauty clinic?

233
19:04.674 --> 19:06.454
I thought you wanted to be a doctor and treat people.

234
19:07.064 --> 19:09.254
Why do you think I like you?

235
19:12.264 --> 19:13.894
It's because you're beautiful.

236
19:14.474 --> 19:15.334
What?

237
19:15.764 --> 19:17.624
You like me because of how I look?

238
19:23.044 --> 19:23.734
Mm.

239
19:25.564 --> 19:28.534
I want you to be my beautiful forever.

240
19:34.054 --> 19:37.704
Then...can I be your only VIP customer forever?

241
19:38.734 --> 19:39.424
Mm.

242
19:40.114 --> 19:41.064
Forever.

243
20:49.774 --> 20:52.754
I'm your first love, Chris.

244
20:58.354 --> 20:59.644
What does that mean?

245
21:01.874 --> 21:05.214
It's a way to bring you back to who you used to be.

246
21:06.984 --> 21:09.404
I never liked it, though.

247
21:11.654 --> 21:13.514
I don't like it either.

248
21:16.654 --> 21:18.464
But it's for your own good.

249
21:22.754 --> 21:24.044
You know

250
21:24.064 --> 21:26.954
I'm willing to do anything for you.

251
21:28.954 --> 21:31.034
What do you smell?

252
21:32.754 --> 21:33.754
Roses...

253
21:35.664 --> 21:36.944
And...

254
21:37.284 --> 21:39.294
Where are you right now?

255
21:41.034 --> 21:42.264
School...

256
21:43.854 --> 21:45.854
What are you doing?

257
21:47.174 --> 21:49.664
Copying my friend's homework.

258
21:50.524 --> 21:52.454
So why did you smell roses?

259
21:58.564 --> 21:59.284
Here.

260
22:01.564 --> 22:02.894
Did you buy these to give to people?

261
22:03.404 --> 22:04.154
No,

262
22:04.174 --> 22:05.354
they're offerings for Buddha.

263
22:07.044 --> 22:09.064
Then no thanks. I don't want to take one meant for Buddha.

264
22:11.104 --> 22:12.774
This one isn't an offering.

265
22:13.604 --> 22:15.224
I want to give it to you.

266
22:16.794 --> 22:18.124
She gave it to me

267
22:18.334 --> 22:20.404
before Buddhism class.

268
22:34.334 --> 22:35.334
Hey, wait!

269
22:35.994 --> 22:36.734
Chris!

270
22:48.864 --> 22:50.584
Have you finished copying my homework?

271
22:51.424 --> 22:53.154
Not yet. Are you going to turn it in now?

272
22:53.904 --> 22:54.704
It's alright.

273
22:54.724 --> 22:56.044
I'll wait until you're done.

274
22:56.764 --> 22:57.694
Give me a sec.

275
23:06.624 --> 23:07.774
Sun...

276
23:09.954 --> 23:11.074
is my friend...?

277
23:22.764 --> 23:23.574
What's wrong?

278
23:30.154 --> 23:33.894
[Third Person]

279
23:36.236 --> 23:38.956
[Third Person]

280
23:42.186 --> 23:43.266
Jeen.

281
23:47.386 --> 23:48.196
Chris.

282
23:49.936 --> 23:50.646
I think

283
23:51.046 --> 23:52.256
Chris needs to rest.

284
24:01.856 --> 24:02.856
Sun...

285
24:03.426 --> 24:04.466
Sun.

286
24:06.366 --> 24:07.366
Chris,

287
24:09.166 --> 24:12.446
will you stop hurting yourself because of that woman?

288
24:23.666 --> 24:25.516
Nadear, I'm at your front door.

289
24:25.536 --> 24:26.926
We should talk.

290
24:27.196 --> 24:28.636
Four years ago,

291
24:29.136 --> 24:30.916
Chris's symptoms were very severe,

292
24:31.396 --> 24:33.046
so you asked me

293
24:33.656 --> 24:36.256
to help Chris live normally.

294
24:41.176 --> 24:41.946
Yes,

295
24:42.856 --> 24:44.736
you helped both Chris

296
24:44.966 --> 24:46.166
and me.

297
24:48.406 --> 24:49.546
Back then, Chris's brain

298
24:49.576 --> 24:52.476
was like a clear, empty glass.

299
24:53.526 --> 24:55.496
Whatever color we add,

300
24:55.826 --> 24:57.556
that's what we'll see.

301
25:00.226 --> 25:02.656
What are you implying?

302
25:03.786 --> 25:06.706
Chris now has her own memories.

303
25:08.286 --> 25:09.896
I'm not sure

304
25:10.176 --> 25:11.746
her body can handle it

305
25:12.396 --> 25:14.036
if we still keep this up.

306
25:15.536 --> 25:17.396
All of Chris's memories

307
25:18.116 --> 25:19.606
are too much

308
25:19.626 --> 25:21.636
for the same clear glass to hold.

309
25:22.566 --> 25:25.436
If remembering everything hurts her,

310
25:27.236 --> 25:30.276
then I want her to remember that much.

311
25:35.346 --> 25:37.956
I can't afford to lose her again.

312
26:00.386 --> 26:02.446
Any updates on the flower dishes?

313
26:10.086 --> 26:12.556
Chris is unwell. I'll tell you later.

314
27:04.366 --> 27:05.416
Chris,

315
27:05.436 --> 27:06.846
are you alright?

316
27:07.366 --> 27:09.036
I'm in front of your house.

317
27:09.536 --> 27:10.796
Can you come see me?

318
27:15.276 --> 27:16.626
[Chris, are you alright?]

319
27:16.656 --> 27:17.776
[I'm in front of your house. Can you come see me?]

320
27:44.556 --> 27:46.876
This really looks like we're having an affair.

321
27:48.836 --> 27:50.456
Why were you gone, then?

322
27:50.616 --> 27:51.956
I couldn't contact you.

323
27:54.596 --> 27:55.946
I'm sick.

324
28:01.566 --> 28:02.776
You don't have a fever, though.

325
28:06.016 --> 28:07.896
I'm a bit dizzy and nauseous.

326
28:08.806 --> 28:10.956
There is a lot to think about right now,

327
28:10.976 --> 28:12.456
so it's affecting my body.

328
28:15.396 --> 28:16.776
Did you think about me too?

329
28:20.166 --> 28:21.056
Yeah.

330
28:22.496 --> 28:23.246
Come on,

331
28:23.266 --> 28:24.466
I thought you'd flirt back

332
28:25.086 --> 28:26.046
and say, "I missed you."

333
28:28.496 --> 28:29.496
Sorry,

334
28:29.746 --> 28:32.036
I'm a bit out of it right now.

335
28:32.656 --> 28:33.936
I couldn't come up with that in time.

336
28:37.656 --> 28:38.856
Is it related to your brain?

337
28:42.026 --> 28:42.956
Yeah.

338
28:43.466 --> 28:44.976
I used to have amnesia.

339
28:46.186 --> 28:48.116
I still can't remember everything,

340
28:49.076 --> 28:50.676
but it's like...

341
28:51.126 --> 28:53.146
my memories are coming back.

342
28:56.456 --> 28:58.166
Would you like to remember?

343
29:00.866 --> 29:01.966
I don't know.

344
29:03.626 --> 29:05.656
Both trying to remember

345
29:05.796 --> 29:08.346
and not being able to remember

346
29:09.776 --> 29:11.396
make me suffer.

347
29:18.726 --> 29:20.046
Why don't you stop thinking about it?

348
29:47.556 --> 29:49.826
If you're happy with how things are now,

349
29:50.956 --> 29:52.546
why not just stay in the present?

350
29:55.526 --> 29:57.446
You really think so?

351
29:58.336 --> 29:59.166
Mm.

352
30:00.056 --> 30:02.456
I lost my dog, whom I loved dearly.

353
30:04.226 --> 30:05.856
My friend felt bad for me,

354
30:06.456 --> 30:08.466
so they gave me a replica dog.

355
30:10.686 --> 30:12.036
When I saw it,

356
30:12.256 --> 30:13.656
it made me even sadder

357
30:15.666 --> 30:17.366
because it reminded me

358
30:17.846 --> 30:19.666
that I'd already lost my dog.

359
30:20.726 --> 30:21.726
A dog?

360
30:22.066 --> 30:23.066
What was their name?

361
30:25.366 --> 30:26.756
"Kiiro."

362
30:31.296 --> 30:32.356
Kiiro?

363
30:34.326 --> 30:35.296
Yes,

364
30:35.326 --> 30:36.566
it means "yellow."

365
30:39.616 --> 30:41.166
My fish is also named "Kiiro."

366
30:50.246 --> 30:51.156
Sun,

367
30:52.916 --> 30:54.466
have we known each other before?

368
31:41.756 --> 31:42.536
Nadear.

369
31:51.286 --> 31:53.446
Why did you go outside without telling me?

370
31:56.416 --> 31:58.036
I just wanted to take a walk.

371
32:01.846 --> 32:02.916
Get some rest.

372
32:16.576 --> 32:19.356
We still have three months, don't we?

373
32:21.556 --> 32:23.156
Less than three months.

374
32:36.186 --> 32:37.336
Look at you.

375
32:37.556 --> 32:39.416
You don't want to be a pretty doctor, huh?

376
32:40.876 --> 32:42.776
I'm still pretty.

377
32:43.726 --> 32:44.356
Yeah, yeah.

378
32:45.116 --> 32:46.396
Why did you do that?

379
32:46.796 --> 32:49.116
Just say the truth and everything will be resolved.

380
32:49.876 --> 32:51.946
I don't understand. Why didn't you tell her?

381
32:53.956 --> 32:56.336
Because the fact that Chris loves me

382
32:57.306 --> 33:01.076
doesn't make what I did right.

383
33:01.806 --> 33:03.256
You weren't the only one at fault.

384
33:03.866 --> 33:06.516
If her memories hurt her...

385
33:08.176 --> 33:10.056
The only thing I want right now

386
33:12.256 --> 33:13.876
is for her to love me.

387
33:18.836 --> 33:20.556
If she loves me,

388
33:20.876 --> 33:23.196
I'll tell her what we used to be.

389
33:25.716 --> 33:27.516
I want to be sure

390
33:29.196 --> 33:30.946
that she will forgive me first.

391
33:36.416 --> 33:37.456
Alright.

392
33:44.016 --> 33:47.216
[Third Person]

393
33:48.175 --> 33:52.265
[Third Person]

394
34:07.025 --> 34:07.875
Nadear...

395
34:30.535 --> 34:32.155
Chris betrayed me.

396
34:34.685 --> 34:37.865
She betrayed me again, Jeen.

397
34:52.645 --> 34:54.985
I lost my dog, whom I loved dearly.

398
34:56.275 --> 34:57.345
A dog?

399
34:57.575 --> 34:58.575
What was their name?

400
35:00.925 --> 35:02.165
Kiiro.

401
35:12.975 --> 35:15.575
Did your name come from the word "yellow" as well?

402
35:16.165 --> 35:17.265
Kiiro.

403
35:36.405 --> 35:37.035
Kiiro...

404
35:37.055 --> 35:38.355
Kiiro is hungry.

405
35:38.575 --> 35:39.575
Come on.

406
35:41.795 --> 35:42.575
Go.

407
35:43.165 --> 35:45.165
Time to eat. Let's go.

408
36:17.035 --> 36:18.055
Nadear...

409
36:19.485 --> 36:20.485
Kiiro...

410
36:32.685 --> 36:34.135
Chris, come eat your breakfast.

411
36:34.285 --> 36:35.965
I made some for you, too.

412
36:38.065 --> 36:38.765
Thanks.

413
36:40.145 --> 36:42.175
Don't forget to take your medicine after your meal.

414
36:47.365 --> 36:48.365
Nadear,

415
36:50.285 --> 36:51.935
where did our dog go?

416
36:54.975 --> 36:56.385
What dog?

417
36:57.475 --> 36:58.875
Our dog.

418
36:59.375 --> 37:02.065
I remember we used to have a dog.

419
37:05.325 --> 37:06.965
Chris, we've never had a dog.

420
37:11.745 --> 37:12.865
We have.

421
37:13.375 --> 37:14.855
Our dog...

422
37:15.815 --> 37:17.065
The other Kiiro.

423
37:24.135 --> 37:24.985
Chris.

424
37:27.375 --> 37:28.555
Listen to me.

425
37:31.065 --> 37:32.755
We've never had a dog.

426
37:37.265 --> 37:39.955
The only possibility is that dog.

427
37:45.715 --> 37:48.485
Nan once asked us to take care of her Corgi.

428
37:49.835 --> 37:52.065
Its fur is brown and white.

429
37:52.755 --> 37:54.945
She left it with us when she flew overseas.

430
37:56.645 --> 37:57.745
It's smart,

431
37:57.765 --> 37:58.865
affectionate,

432
37:59.545 --> 38:01.675
and it likes sitting on your lap.

433
38:05.605 --> 38:06.865
Was it Nan's dog?

434
38:10.285 --> 38:11.175
Yeah.

435
38:20.965 --> 38:22.825
I'll go to the restaurant today, then.

436
38:25.175 --> 38:25.905
Don't.

437
38:25.925 --> 38:27.365
I want you to rest.

438
39:00.775 --> 39:01.495
So this is what

439
39:01.615 --> 39:03.465
you want me to do?

440
39:05.075 --> 39:06.555
To give Chris freedom?

441
39:08.595 --> 39:10.775
To let Chris love someone else?

442
39:13.925 --> 39:16.555
I don't know what to do anymore, Jeen.

443
39:18.485 --> 39:21.875
Even her memories don't seem to be enough to make her mine.

444
39:24.475 --> 39:26.375
Our brains are complex.

445
39:28.645 --> 39:30.365
Chris remembers you,

446
39:30.595 --> 39:32.155
but she still had an affair.

447
39:33.315 --> 39:34.675
Perhaps...

448
39:34.955 --> 39:36.755
her memories alone aren't enough.

449
39:38.625 --> 39:39.955
You first have to know

450
39:40.165 --> 39:41.855
what Chris is planning to do.

451
39:44.485 --> 39:47.065
If I do, Chris will be mine again, right?

452
40:27.985 --> 40:29.375
Welcome, Chris.

453
40:30.555 --> 40:32.255
Can I stay with you tonight?

454
40:33.455 --> 40:35.585
My place is your place.

455
40:51.095 --> 40:52.475
Should I change my hairstyle?

456
40:53.565 --> 40:54.565
Why?

457
40:56.065 --> 40:57.355
I want to be a new me.

458
40:59.705 --> 41:01.075
No need to do that.

459
41:01.725 --> 41:03.165
I like you just the way you are.

460
41:06.165 --> 41:07.265
Thanks.

461
41:15.975 --> 41:17.535
We're friends, so let's stop here.

462
41:20.455 --> 41:22.575
But we've gone a lot further than this.

463
41:27.645 --> 41:30.345
If you realize that, then you should keep a proper distance.

464
41:33.155 --> 41:34.165
Okay.

465
41:36.485 --> 41:38.305
Tonight...

466
41:39.205 --> 41:40.325
Let's just hold hands.

467
41:51.955 --> 41:53.275
Just hold hands.

468
41:54.295 --> 41:56.055
Well, I'm just holding your hand,

469
41:56.405 --> 41:57.655
nothing more.

470
42:00.945 --> 42:03.065
But isn't this too close?

471
42:04.235 --> 42:05.765
Friends can be this close.

472
42:28.335 --> 42:29.335
This is weird.

473
42:29.355 --> 42:31.255
Why did you suddenly ask me to meet you in private?

474
42:31.275 --> 42:32.855
Didn't Nadear say you were sick?

475
42:34.155 --> 42:35.565
Have you ever had a dog?

476
42:37.075 --> 42:38.185
A Corgi.

477
42:39.375 --> 42:40.735
I'm a cat person.

478
42:40.765 --> 42:42.265
I've never had a dog before.

479
42:57.875 --> 42:58.875
Kiiro.

480
42:59.475 --> 43:00.655
Whose dog is it?

481
43:22.985 --> 43:25.615
I don't think it's true that we've never known each other before.

482
43:25.775 --> 43:26.665
Kiiro.

483
43:26.715 --> 43:28.305
It's not a coincidence, right?

484
43:28.455 --> 43:30.175
I just want to know the truth.

485
43:30.365 --> 43:31.685
Who I am right now

486
43:31.705 --> 43:32.825
is the truth.

487
43:33.065 --> 43:34.675
Ever since I lost my memories...

488
43:35.005 --> 43:37.345
Love was just attachment.

489
43:37.425 --> 43:38.685
We should break up.

490
43:38.705 --> 43:40.555
Whoever dares to take Chris away from me

491
43:40.575 --> 43:41.865
will die.

492
43:41.975 --> 43:43.545
To overcome your fear,

493
43:43.565 --> 43:44.745
you'll have to face it.

494
43:44.875 --> 43:46.555
I'll be with you.

495
44:01.965 --> 44:11.885
♫The rain keeps splashing beneath our cover,♫

496
44:11.905 --> 44:17.005
♫Once it was a special place for two lovers♫

497
44:17.025 --> 44:20.905
♫There was never enough room for the third♫

498
44:21.125 --> 44:27.125
♫Now, the rain soaks our hearts together♫

499
44:27.145 --> 44:36.865
♫The question that's trapped in my heart♫

500
44:36.885 --> 44:41.925
♫Maybe it's time for you to do your part♫

501
44:41.945 --> 44:46.225
♫Choose the one your heart truly desires♫

502
44:46.245 --> 44:54.885
♫Before the last raindrop falls, don't make me shed another tear♫

503
44:55.405 --> 45:03.705
♫Before the last raindrop falls, don't make me shed another tear♫
